"11. Keep Nearby", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "entry_block", "target": "ocr_witness_not_truth", "relation": "depends_on", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.85, "source_file": "teaching/machine-assistance/lessons/0006-bt-entry-structuring-from-witnesses.html", "source_location": "1. The Unit Of Work Is The Entry", "weight": 0.85}], "hyperedges": [{"id": "he_bt_entry_foundation", "label": "Entry block, lossless fragments, and schema", "nodes": ["entry_block", "lossless_raw_entry", "dictionary_entry_schema"], "relation": "structuring_foundation", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "teaching/machine-assistance/lessons/0006-bt-entry-structuring-from-witnesses.html", "source_location": "10. Recommended Startup Workflow", "weight": 1.0, "rationale": "The unit of work is the entry, the first representation keeps every fragment and its order, and the Pydantic schema is only a permissive projection of that evidence."}]}